ocation":"Section 'How expected is computed' / AC line 3 ('keyed on expected AND NOT present ... safe to land while the box still has no store')","norm_id":"n082ef77b9e8683a4","priority":0.8,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["First deploy after this change lands: the mcp container has no store yet but expected=true, so the new gate refuses promotion of an otherwise-healthy container — the opposite of the 'inert gate, no flag day' claim the plan sells as the safety story."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Either (a) re-verify the deployed box's env and rewrite the safety section — if the override IS set, the gate is strict today and the change must be paired with provisioning the store, or (b) if the box overrides the compose value to empty, cite that override explicitly since docker-compose.yml:366 shows a non-empty default that would otherwise make expected=true.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"high","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"high","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["2 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable)."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add one contract test that feeds the gate the ACTUAL JSON body produced by the store_status()/health handler (a shared fixture or golden shape), so a key rename in the emitter turns the gate test RED.","cohort":["E3","E5","F4","G5","T6","T9","necessity","project.engine-layer-enforcement","project.portability"],"criteria":["E5"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Health tests live in tests/unit/test_mcp_health_store_status.py; gate tests live in tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_mcp_bluegreen.py — separate suites","AC: 'the gate must read the object and refuse promotion on it' — the emit side and consume side are the seam","No listed test asserts the emitted /health body parses under the exact keys (`store.present`, `store.expected`) the gate reads"],"finding":"The store-object contract is proven on two sides independently (health emits {path,present,expected}; the autodeploy gate refuses on expected AND NOT present) but no test pins that the JSON shape the MCP handler actually emits is exactly the shape the autodeploy gate parses. A key rename or nesting change could keep both suites green while the real curl-fed gate silently fails open (or misparses) in production.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fb659e868810a41a8","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Verification / Per-criterion proving tests table","norm_id":"nc65543c97ba4bac2","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A future refactor renames `present`->`ok` in the handler; the health suite updates to match, the gate suite still uses a canned body with `present`, both stay green, and the real gate fails open on every deploy"],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Derive the autodeploy gate test's /health fixture from the same serialization the handler uses (import the response builder or share a golden JSON), rather than a hand-written body, so emit and consume cannot drift silently.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"Correct the journald citation from docker-compose.yml:72,258,306,383 to the actual lines 72,258,306,409.","cohort":["E4"],"criteria":["E4"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.36,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan quote: 'Container logs use driver: journald at docker-compose.yml:72,258,306,383'","Grep of docker-compose.yml for 'journald' returns lines 72, 258, 306, 409 — not 383"],"finding":"The corroborating journald citation references a line that does not carry the journald driver.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f046db3653e3fe511","impact":0.44,"is_primary":null,"location":"Section 'Evidence' — parenthetical on driver: journald","norm_id":"n39a8e404324bd806","priority":0.44,"reason":"veto:cited-reference-inaccurate","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A reviewer checking line 383 finds no journald directive and may distrust the surrounding evidence."],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Replace ':383' with ':409'.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"no","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"incomplete_enumeration","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Correct the Evidence citation for the blue-green readiness gate from `autodeploy.sh:130` (the MCP_HEALTH_TIMEOUT declaration) to the actual promotion probe at `autodeploy.sh:688` (and the mcp-unhealthy err at :692).","cohort":["G1G2"],"criteria":["G1G2"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.1625,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: `infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh:130` — the blue-green readiness gate promotes on that same probe.","autodeploy.sh:130 is `MCP_HEALTH_TIMEOUT=\"${MCP_HEALTH_TIMEOUT:-120}\" # readiness deadline for the NEW mcp container` (a var declaration, not the gate)","The promotion probe is autodeploy.sh:688 `curl -fsS -m 3 \"http://127.0.0.1:${mcp_newport}/health\" >/dev/null 2>&1` with the mcp-unhealthy err at :692"],"finding":"The Evidence bullet cites `infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh:130` as the blue-green readiness gate that 'promotes on that same probe', but line 130 is the `MCP_HEALTH_TIMEOUT` env-var definition. The actual MCP readiness/promotion probe is `curl -fsS -m 3 \"http://127.0.0.1:${mcp_newport}/health\" >/dev/null` at line 688, whose failure triggers the `mcp-unhealthy` err at line 692 (the reason string the AC references).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f22e5f703741d3aa9","impact":0.85,"is_primary":null,"location":"Evidence — `infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh:130`","norm_id":"n890ca756f024c684","priority":0.6375,"reason":"veto:cited-reference-inaccurate","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An implementer follows the cited line to make the gate consume the new store object and edits the wrong location (the timeout constant) instead of the readiness loop at :686-695."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Replace the `autodeploy.sh:130` evidence line with `infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh:688` (the `curl -fsS ... /health >/dev/null` readiness probe; failure raises `mcp-unhealthy` at :692).","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"no","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_alt